course: dictionary
lesson: 12400
title: Cutting it short
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To curtail something is to cut it short, or to make it smaller or less. You can curtail a visit, a trip or a holiday, which means it ends sooner than planned. «The match was curtailed by heavy rain.» The game stopped early because of the rain, so curtailed means cut short.
explain: Curtail can also mean to limit someone's freedom or power. «The new rules curtailed how long we could play games after school.» The rules made our playing time smaller, so curtail means reduce or limit. The word often shows that something was done against people's wishes.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Ask: did something end early, or get smaller? If yes, curtail probably means cut or limit. Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Curtail is a formal word, so you will often meet it in the news and in serious writing.
fact: «Curtail» means to cut something short or make it smaller.
fact: «Curtailed» means cut short, as in «a holiday curtailed by storms».
fact: «Curtail» can also mean to limit someone's freedom or power.
fact: Things people often curtail include visits, trips, holidays, spending, rights and activities.
exercise: «The school trip was curtailed when the bus broke down.» What does curtailed mean here? | Painted bright red | *Cut short | Made longer | Cheered loudly
exercise: «The council decided to curtail spending on new toys.» What is being made smaller? | The weather | *Spending | The council | The toys
exercise: «The storm curtailed our picnic before we had eaten lunch.» Find and copy the word that means cut short. | lunch | storm | *curtailed | picnic
test: «The new rules curtailed how long we could play online.» What does curtailed mean? | *Limited or reduced | Celebrated | Made longer | Forgotten
test: «Her holiday was curtailed by a phone call from home.» What does this tell you? | She ate a big meal | *Her holiday ended early | Her holiday became bigger | Her holiday went on for ever
exam: Ruby reads «The king curtailed the power of the nobles.» Which word is closest in meaning to curtailed? | helped | celebrated | *limited | painted
